Volume I: System Architecture & Data Flow
Layered Architecture Pattern (Separation of Concerns)

Dependency Inversion (Transport Agnosticism)

The Request Lifecycle:

Routers: Route multiplexing and endpoint definition.

Middleware: Request interception, fail-fast mechanics, and Zod validation.

Controllers: HTTP transport adapters (handling req/res).

Services: Pure business logic and database interactions.

Serializers (DTOs): Data filtering to prevent sensitive information leakage.

Volume II: Database Engineering & ORM Mechanics
PostgreSQL Fundamentals: Tables, rows, columns, Primary Keys, and Foreign Keys.

Database Infrastructure: Local development vs. Cloud (Neon, Supabase, AWS RDS).

Query Optimization:

The Offset Penalty (Why LIMIT/OFFSET fails at scale).

Keyset/Cursor Pagination (The enterprise solution).

Text Search (Op.iLike vs. Trigram Indexes).

Sequelize ORM:

Models, Migrations, and Seeders.

Abstract Syntax Trees (ASTs) and SQL compilation.

The N+1 Query Problem and Eager Loading.

Associations: hasOne, hasMany, belongsTo.

Data Security: UUIDs (Universally Unique Identifiers) vs. Standard Sequential IDs (preventing Enumeration/IDOR attacks).

Volume III: Applied Cryptography
Encryption vs. Hashing (Two-way vs. One-way functions).

Rainbow Tables and pre-computed hash attacks.

Cryptographic Salting to ensure unique hashes for identical passwords.

Bcrypt: Key stretching and algorithmic cost factors to prevent GPU brute-forcing.

Volume IV: The JavaScript Event Loop
Execution Models: Synchronous (Blocking) vs. Asynchronous (Non-Blocking) execution.

Node.js Architecture:

The single-threaded V8 Call Stack.

The libuv C++ library and the background Worker Pool.

The Task Queue and the Event Loop monitoring cycle.

Modern JS Standards: const vs. let, Array methods (map, filter), and ESLint for codebase uniformity.

Naming Conventions: camelCase, PascalCase, and snake_case.

Volume V: Identity & Access Architecture
Stateless Authentication (JWT - JSON Web Tokens):

Header, Payload (Claims), and Signature math.

Base64Url Encoding vs. Encryption.

The "Fatal Flaw" (inability to revoke).

The Access + Refresh Token pattern to secure JWTs.

Stateful Authentication (Redis Opaque Tokens):

In-memory Key-Value storage for lightning-fast lookups.

Instant session revocation and global lockouts.

Token Storage: LocalStorage (XSS vulnerabilities) vs. HttpOnly Cookies (Enterprise standard).

Authorization: RBAC (Role-Based Access Control) vs. ABAC (Attribute-Based Access Control).

Volume VI: Network Protocol & API Contracts
REST Operations: GET, POST, PUT, DELETE.

Network State Mutations & Idempotency:

Safe methods vs. Idempotent mutations vs. Non-Idempotent mutations.

Idempotency Keys (The Stripe Pattern) for safe network retries.

Exhaustive HTTP Status Codes:

1xx: Informational (Protocol handshakes).

2xx: Success (200 OK, 201 Created, 204 No Content).

3xx: Redirection (Caching and routing).

4xx: Client Errors (400 Bad Request, 401 Unauthorized, 403 Forbidden, 409 Conflict, 429 Too Many Requests).

5xx: Server Errors (500 Internal Server Error, 502 Bad Gateway, 504 Gateway Timeout).



